{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Like these you shall make for the seven days.</b> Above, in the priestly Torah in the parashah of Emor, which deals with matters of the Land — as I explained there — it mentions the festivals and the grains customarily associated with them; therefore it mentions the offerings brought on account of the omer and the two breads. But here it mentions only the offerings brought on account of the day." "<b>And their libations.</b> It refers back to 'לחם אשה' (a grain offering of fire) that precedes it, and these are wine libations and meal-offering libations."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:05.346326489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}